{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1540348-da-v-flesh-of-the-corpse-flaw-question","id":1540348,"title":"DA:V Flesh of the Corpse Flaw question","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-08-14T05:42:15-07:00","id":1540348,"title":"DA:V Flesh of the Corpse Flaw question","content":"Flesh of the Corpse (p.304 DA:V) states:<br /> \u201dYour flesh does not fully regenerate itself once it is damaged. While you are able to heal yourself to the point of regaining full functionality, your skin still retains the cuts, tears and wounds you have incurred. Depending on the nature of the damage, this Flaw will make social dealings exceedingly difficult.\u201d<br /> <br /> I was wondering if Vicissitude could be used to close/knit/patch over the broken skin.<br /> Thoughts would be appreciated.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I had a conscience once. Alas, I appear to have misplaced it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1309-andreas-rayne","name":"Andreas Rayne","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-14T07:27:26-07:00","id":1540353,"title":"","content":"I would say yes, you can repeair the damage but it would return like the Nosferatu disfigurment at next day. Flaw for a reason<br /> Realistically speaking there is not much of the skin that is visible just the hands and the face maybe part of the chest, so putting extra skin on it like a patch would be noticable and disturbing - but a Master could do it, finding the perfect skin tone, the fine work, etc. A work of art - frankly too much work to worht your time - but that wouldn't be the part of your body, like a piercing or tattoo the body would reject it in the next day (except if he Tzismice woudl tear off the skin lets say from your ass to use your own skin as the patch, untill you wear a literall skin-mask<br /> But I would allow to &quot;buy out&quot; the flaw with XP","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-14T07:34:03-07:00","id":1540354,"title":"","content":"I'd be inclined to say yes, although probably with a slightly higher degree of difficulty on the Dexterity + Body Craft roll.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-14T14:50:35-07:00","id":1540388,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1540348-da-v-flesh-of-the-corpse-flaw-question?p=1540353#post1540353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would say yes, you can repeair the damage but it would return like the Nosferatu disfigurment at next day. Flaw for a reason<br /> Realistically speaking there is not much of the skin that is visible just the hands and the face maybe part of the chest, so putting extra skin on it like a patch would be noticable and disturbing - but a Master could do it, finding the perfect skin tone, the fine work, etc. A work of art - frankly too much work to worht your time - but that wouldn't be the part of your body, like a piercing or tattoo the body would reject it in the next day (except if he Tzismice woudl tear off the skin lets say from your ass to use your own skin as the patch, untill you wear a literall skin-mask<br /> But I would allow to &quot;buy out&quot; the flaw with XP</div> </div> </div> </div>That\u2019s great. Thank you very much.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I had a conscience once. Alas, I appear to have misplaced it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1309-andreas-rayne","name":"Andreas Rayne","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-14T14:51:27-07:00","id":1540390,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1540348-da-v-flesh-of-the-corpse-flaw-question?p=1540354#post1540354\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd be inclined to say yes, although probably with a slightly higher degree of difficulty on the Dexterity + Body Craft roll.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fantastic. Thank you very much.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I had a conscience once. Alas, I appear to have misplaced it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1309-andreas-rayne","name":"Andreas Rayne","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-14T18:22:29-07:00","id":1540402,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Andreas Rayne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1540348-da-v-flesh-of-the-corpse-flaw-question#post1540348\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Flesh of the Corpse (p.304 DA:V) states:<br /> \u201dYour flesh does not fully regenerate itself once it is damaged. While you are able to heal yourself to the point of regaining full functionality, your skin still retains the cuts, tears and wounds you have incurred. Depending on the nature of the damage, this Flaw will make social dealings exceedingly difficult.\u201d<br /> <br /> I was wondering if Vicissitude could be used to close/knit/patch over the broken skin.<br /> Thoughts would be appreciated.</div> </div> </div> </div>I strongly doubt it that a Vicissitude could fix such issues otherwise the Nosferatu and the more hideous members of the Cappodocians would have sought them out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-15T08:37:24-07:00","id":1540434,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1540348-da-v-flesh-of-the-corpse-flaw-question?p=1540402#post1540402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I strongly doubt it that a Vicissitude could fix such issues otherwise the Nosferatu and the more hideous members of the Cappodocians would have sought them out.</div> </div> </div> </div>Those are Clan weaknesses resulting from Caine cursing the Clan's founder. Flesh of the Corpse is just a physical flaw that is, presumably, a glitch in the vampire's ability to heal themselves and is mostly cosmetic. All you are doing with Vicissitude is joining skin back together and trying to cover up places where the skin might have been burnt or otherwise destroyed. This may require trying to patch new skin (taken from living or dead donors) over certain areas, which probably won't match perfectly. The longer this goes on and the more damage you have to fix, the more the social difficulty penalties are going to stack up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-15T12:07:34-07:00","id":1540447,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't allow any Flaw to be permanently overcome through normal gameplay alone. They provided build points during character creation, and it would be unfair to other PCs to simply let a PC get those points for free and ignore the Flaw going forward.<br /> <br /> Therefore in a situation like this, I'd be very hesitant as an ST to allow Vicissitude to negate a Flaw like this even though it seems it would be appropriate. A player just shouldn't be able to ignore the Flaws they took for their PC. A Flaw like that, IMO, isn't just a &quot;glitch&quot; that is cosmetic. It indicates some kind of deep rooted supernatural defect in the vampire's being. Why? Who knows? They just happen. Like any other kind of Flaw. I don't care if it's not from the Curse of Caine himself.<br /> <br /> However, Flaws can be bought off with XP. So if I was going to allow a PC to overcome that Flaw by whatever means or flavor text, I'd always make the PC spend XP to remove that Flaw permanently. Otherwise, it's going to keep coming up in play. I'd probably require something more than just using Vicissitude though. Some additional arduous, difficult, or unique event would have to come up as well. Let the player do the heavy work of coming up with that concept, running it by me as the ST, and I'll approve it if I like it and work with the player for that situation to come up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-15T12:27:36-07:00","id":1540455,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1540348-da-v-flesh-of-the-corpse-flaw-question?p=1540434#post1540434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Those are Clan weaknesses resulting from Caine cursing the Clan's founder. Flesh of the Corpse is just a physical flaw that is, presumably, a glitch in the vampire's ability to heal themselves and is mostly cosmetic. All you are doing with Vicissitude is joining skin back together and trying to cover up places where the skin might have been burnt or otherwise destroyed. This may require trying to patch new skin (taken from living or dead donors) over certain areas, which probably won't match perfectly. The longer this goes on and the more damage you have to fix, the more the social difficulty penalties are going to stack up.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good point and I should've mentioned that maybe it wouldn't work if the flaw was of a weird supernatural origin and the Disciplines wouldn't work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-15T18:24:59-07:00","id":1540489,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1540348-da-v-flesh-of-the-corpse-flaw-question?p=1540447#post1540447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldn't allow any Flaw to be permanently overcome through normal gameplay alone. They provided build points during character creation, and it would be unfair to other PCs to simply let a PC get those points for free and ignore the Flaw going forward.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>While I agree with you, I'd consider this working if getting the help of a Vicissitude user isn't a negligible task. Getting this help may be costly enough that for all purposes the flaw is still causing trouble, as it is intended to do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-15T19:36:37-07:00","id":1540496,"title":"","content":"If nothing else, I would presume it to involve the whole Kindred culture of trading favors/Boons. Even if it's another PC doing it for you, you should have to owe them a comparable favor or compensation down the line.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-16T17:58:20-07:00","id":1540537,"title":"","content":"I would say <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar23890_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"23890\" data-vbnamecard=\"23890\">Shadeprowler</a> and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3046\" data-vbnamecard=\"3046\">Black Fox</a> are providing answers in the spirit of the game; it is reasonable to temporarily negate the deleterious effects of a Flaw (in this case through Vicissitude), but it is a Flaw for a reason. And buying off the Flaw shouldn't just be a case of spending experience points, but should represent a significant event in character development.<br /> <br /> Another one, I think, for the <i>Vampire: the Dark Ages</i> FAQ and errata. I promise I will properly put it together at some point...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/317-james_willoughby","name":"James_Willoughby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar317_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-21T00:38:57-07:00","id":1540826,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>James_Willoughby</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1540348-da-v-flesh-of-the-corpse-flaw-question?p=1540537#post1540537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would say <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar23890_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"23890\" data-vbnamecard=\"23890\">Shadeprowler</a> and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3046\" data-vbnamecard=\"3046\">Black Fox</a> are providing answers in the spirit of the game; it is reasonable to temporarily negate the deleterious effects of a Flaw (in this case through Vicissitude), but it is a Flaw for a reason. And buying off the Flaw shouldn't just be a case of spending experience points, but should represent a significant event in character development.<br /> <br /> Another one, I think, for the <i>Vampire: the Dark Ages</i> FAQ and errata. I promise I will properly put it together at some point...</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019ll keep my eyes peeled. Thanks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I had a conscience once. Alas, I appear to have misplaced it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1309-andreas-rayne","name":"Andreas Rayne","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-24T14:39:51-07:00","id":1540972,"title":"","content":"I'd allow it, with all the caveats and consequences dealing with Tzimisce for favors generally entails. It wouldn't prevent further mutilation past that point which would necessitate going to a fleshcrafter <i>again</i>, it is still a flaw. I'd rule the difficulty for the fleshcrafting roll would be the same as raising Appearance (as that's effectively what's being done), though.<br /> <br /> But generally, players take flaws like that when they <i>want</i> to be a horrifically-mutilated corpse -- and have other outs for dealing with mortals and/or existing largely separate from them. It's a dark ages flaw, and preventing/dealing with silence of the blood breaches is generally far easier than modern nights <i>masquerade</i> breaches.<br /> <br /> &quot;Disciplines shouldn't override flaws&quot; is kind of a non-starter argument against it, because if you're asking it in the case of this particular interaction, you should start asking it of <i>all</i> interactions...and that's a rabbit hole most players are loathe to go down. The nosferatu have two clan disciplines that &quot;override&quot; their clan flaw in one way or another, just for starters, but at the same time not having those disciplines makes the clan prohibitively difficult to play.<br /> <br /> But, the flaw itself is designed in kind of a silly way and is honestly redundant. It has no in-built mechanics for how to handle mortal interactions, nor losing Appearance over time as would be the logical outcome of such a flaw. I've never seen anyone take it, because if a player wants to go that route they generally take monstrous, visage of death, or...whatever the Cappadocian version of monstrous was called. Both conveniently equal the same five freebie points, have the same effect taken together, and come with in-built mechanics (hence the redundancy).<br /> <br /> The only use case for it by my estimation, would be for a metamorphosist Tzimisce character as a narrative impulse to be a metamorphosist in the first place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-24T18:19:00-07:00","id":1540980,"title":"","content":"I would allow it to function, but only for a single scene, after which the flesh would begin peeling apart. Basically the player could temporarily negate the social penalties of the flaw for a scene by spending a blood point, which I feel is reasonably balanced. Blood is generally a precious commodity and a player might find themself needing to spend 4 or 5 blood points to negate their flaw for a night, depending on what happens. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-28T20:37:25-07:00","id":1541164,"title":"","content":"I'm in agreement with Black Fox et al. A Flaw is a Flaw. It's worth XP. You can't just use Disciplines to get rid of it. Especially since, if some in this thread have forgotten, PCs can be Tzimisce at chargen. If a member of the coterie's player dumps two of their starting Discipline dots in Vicissitude, they could <i>mend the damage from the word go</i>.<br /> <br /> Pretty sure that's not Rules As Intended.<br /> <br /> I'm fully on board with the player using the fleshcrafting to buy off their Flaw with XP. Much like how I'm fine with Mage characters using Magick to buy off Flaws or boost their Attributes on a permanent basis. The point is for the scales to be balanced at the end of the day. The player grabbed a lump sum of XP at chargen, and now how to live with the consequences until they pay that debt back.<br /> <br /> Speaking of, I disagree with the idea that owing Debt to another vampire is, itself, sufficient cost to remove a Flaw. Sure, there's a loss of social capital relative to that Cainite. But outside Elysium (or the Dark Ages equivalent), this doesn't come up in night-to-night operation. Until the Tzimisce chooses to call in that Boon, for normal gameplay, the fix <i>might as well be free</i>.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, being down a single dot in an Attribute, Ability, or Discipline, because you didn't take that Flaw, IS going to come up often enough from session to session. Often enough to create bad feelings if the one player got to escape the primary price for their &quot;loan&quot;, and another player didn't.<br /> <br /> <br /> (As an aside, I do like the idea of a player taking the Flaw, with the intent of making curing it the focus of their immediate character arc. They need to find a way to slip their &quot;curse&quot;, which becomes a Story unto itself. But that's something the player and Storyteller need to hash out together, before play starts.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-28T22:40:14-07:00","id":1541168,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1540348-da-v-flesh-of-the-corpse-flaw-question?p=1541164#post1541164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm in agreement with Black Fox et al. A Flaw is a Flaw. It's worth XP. You can't just use Disciplines to get rid of it. Especially since, if some in this thread have forgotten, PCs can be Tzimisce at chargen. If a member of the coterie's player dumps two of their starting Discipline dots in Vicissitude, they could <i>mend the damage from the word go</i>.<br /> <br /> Pretty sure that's not Rules As Intended.<br /> <br /> I'm fully on board with the player using the fleshcrafting to buy off their Flaw with XP. Much like how I'm fine with Mage characters using Magick to buy off Flaws or boost their Attributes on a permanent basis. The point is for the scales to be balanced at the end of the day. The player grabbed a lump sum of XP at chargen, and now how to live with the consequences until they pay that debt back.<br /> <br /> Speaking of, I disagree with the idea that owing Debt to another vampire is, itself, sufficient cost to remove a Flaw. Sure, there's a loss of social capital relative to that Cainite. But outside Elysium (or the Dark Ages equivalent), this doesn't come up in night-to-night operation. Until the Tzimisce chooses to call in that Boon, for normal gameplay, the fix <i>might as well be free</i>.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, being down a single dot in an Attribute, Ability, or Discipline, because you didn't take that Flaw, IS going to come up often enough from session to session. Often enough to create bad feelings if the one player got to escape the primary price for their &quot;loan&quot;, and another player didn't.<br /> <br /> <br /> (As an aside, I do like the idea of a player taking the Flaw, with the intent of making curing it the focus of their immediate character arc. They need to find a way to slip their &quot;curse&quot;, which becomes a Story unto itself. But that's something the player and Storyteller need to hash out together, before play starts.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I have three problems with such a rigid take.<br /> <br /> For one, the flaw isn't cured in any way by this method. What it does is let things &quot;reset&quot;, at least partially, from time to time, which works as a means of keeping the proposed dynamics going. Without it, the player has no incentive to risk literal skin in the beginning, nor has reason to care after a time.<br /> <br /> Second, it is a very narrow understanding of what a Flaw is. The purpose of a Flaw is to give the character problems that add drama to the story. What exactly those problems entails doesn't have to be set on stone. If the player wants to get rid of one thing, give it a steep price. If the player finds a way to get rid of the initial mechanic, but that requires constant effort, the Flaw achieved its purpose.<br /> <br /> Third and last, it ignores that this particular Flaw, if taken to its natural conclusion, will either be an impediment to most games, if the character becomes monstrously mauled, or will be completely irrelevant due to Obfuscate, which already does exactly the same thing: trivializes the whole problem with a relatively accessible power.<br /> <br /> At no point am I advocating for eliminating the Flaw with a power. I'm advocating for dealing with the Flaw creatively, so it becomes more fun and usable at the table.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-29T00:24:01-07:00","id":1541181,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1540348-da-v-flesh-of-the-corpse-flaw-question?p=1541168#post1541168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The purpose of a Flaw is to give the character problems that add drama to the story.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I agree that the purpose of a Flaw <i>should</i> be to add drama that the player <i>wants</i> for her PC, I've seen way too many players pick Flaws simply for the build points. They actually become angry if an ST uses their Flaws as plot complications (or if other players remind them of such). The game quickly does not become fun for them. <br /> <br /> Granted I've seen this most often in LARP instead of tabletop, but that's probably because my tabletop games are heavily curated to be only those players with whom I know I have a compatible gaming style, while LARP is usually with anyone who walks in from the street. So while among my gaming group this is not a problem, I do think a large number of general gamers view Flaws as just an excuse to get more build points and they never bring them up into play. When STs start incorporating them into game, they begin looking for ways to get rid of their Flaws. And if you allow them cheap ways to eliminate them (especially by not requiring them to spend XP), they'll do it.<br /> <br /> If you allow those kind of players to get away with getting free build points, it is extremely unfair to the other players.<br /> <br /> I actually don't think you are arguing that much with others and myself though. I think it's a minor clarification you are making because the above has not been a problem for you. Others have different experiences though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-29T08:54:37-07:00","id":1541199,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1540348-da-v-flesh-of-the-corpse-flaw-question?p=1541181#post1541181\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> While I agree that the purpose of a Flaw <i>should</i> be to add drama that the player <i>wants</i> for her PC, I've seen way too many players pick Flaws simply for the build points. They actually become angry if an ST uses their Flaws as plot complications (or if other players remind them of such). The game quickly does not become fun for them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've had my share of such players, though I admit it wasn't too common. In my personal experience the fear that this will happen is usually greater than the frequency of it actually happening.<br /> <br /> Not here or there, though, the fact that such players will stop having fun is even more of a reason to not be too strict for me. Instead, I prefer to talk to the players about the issue and find some common ground. So it's less that I don't see the problem and more that I disagree with the solution.<br /> <br /> Then again, for whatever it's worth, I don't play LARP.<br /> <br /> Either way I personally prefer CoD's take on Flaws (Persistent Conditions) than the usual point-based, so I see this system as, no pun intended, flawed anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}